# Admin UI standards (content only)

Ignore top nav / side nav when matching mockups. Style **main content** only.

## Source of truth

- Global CSS: `styles/admin-shell.css` under `[data-admin-shell]`
- Shared chrome: `components/dashboard/AdminPageShell.tsx`
- Form utilities: `components/dashboard/dashboardFormStyles.tsx`
- Layout padding: `DashboardLayout` → `.admin-content-frame` (15px / 20px lg, full width)

## Do

- Prefer CSS tokens / utility classes from admin-shell over one-off page styles
- Use `AdminPageHeader`, `AdminCard`, `AdminKpiGrid` / `AdminKpiCard`, `AdminFilterBar`, `AdminTableShell`, `AdminStatusPill`, `AdminDetailLayout` for new or heavily edited screens
- Primary actions: yellow `#E1BB33` (`btn-admin-primary` / `Button` default / `primaryButtonClass`)
- Outline secondary: white + gray border (`btn-admin-outline` / `outlineButtonClass`)
- Titles `#4F5077`, muted `#6B7A99`, cards white rounded-2xl, fields rounded-xl
- Keep Coaches (in-house, `registration_source=admin`) separate from Online Coaches (`self`)

## Don't

- Don't restyle every page individually for the same look — extend `admin-shell.css` instead
- Don't add max-width content wrappers (`max-w-7xl`, `max-w-6xl`, `mx-auto`) — content is full width under `.admin-content-frame`
- Don't add extra page-level `p-4` / `lg:px-8` — frame already pads 15–20px
- Don't mix Online Coach CTAs (Approvals / Availability / Subscriptions) into in-house Coaches pages
- Don't change public/marketing pages (outside `[data-admin-shell]`)
